  "answer": "Project Zenith is a cloud storage optimization initiative aimed at enhancing security and accessibility, led by Marcus Cole. The project kicked off in July 2023 and has successfully completed its design and testing phases, with a prototype for secure file sharing tested ahead of schedule. The team is now moving into the development phase, led by Omar Jensen, with a focus on user interface enhancements starting in October. To support this, five new members specializing in cybersecurity and cloud architecture joined the team in September, and a training budget of $15,000 was approved for the coding team and project managers. The executive board approved a total project budget of $2 million, though an update noted an adjustment to $550,000 due to unforeseen expenses. The team is also exploring a partnership with TechInnovate for AI technology. A milestone celebration for the completion of the testing phase is scheduled for October 10th."
